          "thinking": "Now I need to understand what acompose and umbra actually are. The key references I need:\n\n1. `contracting-offers.md` - \"Speaking palette for Kai's contracting conversations - the buyer-side framing of each headline project, five cells each, plus which cells convert.\" This is directly relevant - it has umbra pitch, mcp-beaver pitch, agent-compose pitch (acompose).\n\n2. `portfolio.md` - the current portfolio lanes, four committed headlines.\n\n3. `saas-wedges.md` - twelve SaaS wedges.\n\n4. `business-disposition.md` - founding impulse.\n\nLet me load these. The most directly relevant to \"what would someone pay for a custom cut + support\" is contracting-offers.md (buyer-side framing of each headline project, which cells convert) and portfolio.md.\n\nAlso I need to understand: is acompose = agent-compose? \"acompose\" is likely \"agent-compose\". And umbra is a separate headline project.\n\nLet me load contracting-offers.md, portfolio.md, saas-wedges.md, and business-disposition.md.\n\nThe comp rule: \"$150 an hour rule rate\" is confirmed. This is the anchor for the \"one-time cut\" pricing (hours × $150). And 70% utilisation.\n\nSo the price bands will be built from: hours estimate × $150/hr for the one-time cut, plus a monthly support retainer. But I must be careful not to invent. The rule rate is $150/hr confirmed. The long-term support = retainer, which is an invented number unless I derive from the rate and some hour assumption.\n\nLet me read the project references first.",
