                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "1.\ntitle       Create custom subagents - Claude Code Docs\nhref        https://code.claude.com/docs/en/sub-agents\nbody        Create and use specialized AI subagents in Claude Code for task-specific\n            workflows and improved context management.\n2.\ntitle       Claude Code Agents & Subagents: The Complete Guide\nhref        https://skillsplayground.com/guides/claude-code-agents/\nbody        Master Claude Code agents and subagents. Learn how agents work, how to create\n            custom subagents, use the Agent SDK, and build autonomous multi-\n            agent workflows for complex coding tasks.\n3.\ntitle       Claude Code Subagents: The Complete Guide to Building Custom ...\nhref        https://www.aiforanything.io/blog/claude-code-subagents-tutorial-2026\nbody        Jul 2, 2026 · Learn how Claude Code subagents work and how to build your own —\n            YAML frontmatter, tool restrictions, model selection, and real-\n            world examples for 2026.\n4.\ntitle       GitHub - chusri/claude-code-agents: A collection of ...\nhref        https://github.com/chusri/claude-code-agents\nbody        This repository contains 75 specialized subagents that extend Claude Code's\n            capabilities. Each subagent is an expert in a specific domain,\n            automatically invoked based on context or explicitly called when\n            needed.\n5.\ntitle       Claude Agents: Comprehensive Guide - Understanding and ...\nhref        https://gist.github.com/bartsmykla/d7dfca753dae6d20cd58b018b0d7c6dd\nbody        Oct 31, 2025 · Claude agents (also called subagents) are specialized\n            autonomous workers that Claude can spawn to handle specific tasks.\n            Think of them as focused experts that Claude delegates work to -\n            similar to how a senior engineer might delegate specific tasks to\n            specialists on their team.\n=====Q2=====\n1.\ntitle       Services | Invariant Labs\nhref        https://invariantlabs.co/services\nbody        Book a call for a custom proposal. Explore Invariant Labs AI automation,\n            research assistant, custom dashboard, and enterprise roadmap\n            services.\n2.\ntitle       Invariant Labs Review: Features, Use Cases & Pricing 2026\nhref        https://theseaitools.com/tools/invariant-labs\nbody        Invariant Labs publishes current plan, usage, trial, cloud, or enterprise\n            information on its official website. Review the latest pricing\n            before adopting it because product packaging and limits can\n            change.\n3.\ntitle       Invariant Labs Review: Features, Use Cases & Pricing 2026\nhref        https://theseaitools.com/tools/invariant-labs-ai\nbody        Invariant Labs pricing can change over time, and TheseAItools does not publish\n            live billing data for every listing. Check the official website\n            for the latest plan names, limits, and availability.\n4.\ntitle       Invariant Labs – Monitoring and Security: Features, Use Cases ...\nhref        https://www.techbible.ai/tool/invariant-labs\nbody        Security and observability tools for AI agents and LLM applications. Use\n            cases: Securing AI agents against malicious behaviors, Monitoring\n            and debugging LLM applications, Detecting and preventing prompt\n            injection attacks. Discover Invariant Labs features, pricing,\n            integrations, and top alternatives.\n5.\ntitle       Invariant Labs - Excellence in Blockchain Development\nhref        https://dev.invariant.app/\nbody        Invariant has shown themselves to be a professional and dependable DeFi team.\n            They were the first on Eclipse to implement large-scale Pyth price\n            feeds as part of their points system, which was used by over 150k\n            users.\n=====Q3=====\n1.\ntitle       How to Price an AI Agent Retainer (And Turn One-Off Builds Into Recurring\n            Revenue) | Duet Blog\nhref        https://duet.so/blog/turn-ai-agent-builds-into-recurring-retainers\nbody        July 3, 2026 - A retainer for AI agent work is a monthly fee — typically\n            $1,000-$5,000/mo for solo consultants and small shops — covering\n            hosting, monitoring, and a fixed slice of iteration, priced as a\n            floor rate plus a stated overage policy, not a flat ...\n2.\ntitle       AI Agent Pricing Models Explained (2026) | Pickaxe\nhref        https://pickaxe.co/post/ai-agent-pricing-models\nbody        April 28, 2026 - If any answer is \"no\" or \"maybe,\" stick with usage or\n            subscription. If you're a consultant or agency, the range is\n            $300–$1,500/month per client for a deployed agent handling a\n            specific workflow.\n3.\ntitle       AI Consulting Rate: A Breakdown of Hourly, Project, and Retainer Models\nhref        https://www.orientsoftware.com/blog/ai-consultant-hourly-rate/\nbody        August 20, 2025 - Light-touch support, including model performance reviews and\n            checks and strategic check-ins. The cost of this support can be\n            between $1,500 to $5,000 per month, depending on the hourly rate\n            of the consultant and expertise.\n4.\ntitle       AI Consulting Pricing Models for CRE Firms 2026\nhref        https://www.theaiconsultingnetwork.com/blog/ai-consulting-pricing-models-hourly-project-retainer-cre-2026\nbody        April 10, 2026 - A typical progression is a small hourly engagement ($500 to\n            $1,500) to evaluate opportunities, followed by a project\n            engagement ($3,000 to $8,000) to build core workflows, then an\n            optional retainer ($500 to $1,500 per month) for ongoing support.\n5.\ntitle       AI Agent Maintenance and Support Plans: Monthly Costs Explained\nhref        https://www.abbacustechnologies.com/ai-agent-maintenance-and-support-plans-monthly-costs-explained/\nbody        2 days ago - Current market examples show that basic AI agent monitoring\n            retainers can begin around several hundred dollars per month,\n            while maintenance plus engineering support can reach several\n            thousand dollars monthly. One published 2026 maintenance offering,\n            for example, lists monitoring from $500 per ...",
